  "fields": {
    "title": "Hyperlink",
    "textContent": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Description",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "One of the most iconic elements of the web is the ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "hyperlink",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ", which links to other webpages similar to cross-references. Hyperlinks are made possible by the anchor element (<a>). This HTML tag  with its ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "href",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " attribute, creates not only hyperlinks to web pages, but also files, email addresses, or locations in the same page – anything a URL can address. The href attribute should indicate the link's destination, so when you click the anchor element, you will be send to this specific URL. This doesn't have to be another website, it could also be something like an email address or a telephone number. The ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "href ",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "opens in this cases your default mail program or phone app to write a mail to this email address or call this phone number.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "The anchor element can not only include ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "href",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ", but also attributes like ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "download, rel, target, type",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " or",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " referrerpolicy",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ". A common hyperlink attribute next to href is ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "target=\"_blank\"",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ", which opens the link in a new browser tab. ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Download",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " is also quite useful to treat the linked URL (mostly files such as images, pdfs or zips) as a download.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Background",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "The web was developed by Tim Berners-Lee to be able to distribute the documents of his colleagues and other academics and make them accessible to all within his institute at CERN using the internet. He also wanted to be able to link them to each other and therefore set them in relation to each other. That's why he invented HTML. HTML initially only included the ability to display ASCII text and hyperlinks, as these functions were most essential to him. The hyperlink not only plays a crucial role of the concept of ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "3yOBecAoV11TC0Y5c4tReo",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "hypertext",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ", but is also an important part of our culture today.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Possibilities",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Originally hyperlinks were styled as blue underlined text, so they could be easily recognized. But of course they don't have to look this way, even if this default styling has it's own ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "7aP7WpcrLnybp7ybP2w5Cf",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "brutalist",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " charme. There are e.g. different ways to ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "34zBWBy5HyBNj7sYQbx1TN",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "underline text",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " and a lot of possibilities for ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "5Kqa2ZyANgkNAtfUxAU1KP",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "hover",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " effects, especially with ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "1dmTPt3ONqIzoLPuoDUMuT",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "variable fonts",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ". But keep in mind, that the user should be possible to recognize a hyperlink as an interactive element.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
